          "role": "tool_result",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "115\t\\paragraph{Metric constraints on trained--reference comparison.}\n116\tTrained models produce action outputs, enabling Cohen's $d$ on action MSE (OpenVLA, TraceVLA) or cosine distance on action tokens (NORA).\n117\tReference VLMs (Phi-3-Vision, Qwen2.5-VL) do not generate actions; their sensitivity is measured via cosine distance on hidden representations---a metric with different scale, units, and distributional properties.\n118\tRatios between Cohen's $d$ and cosine distance are therefore methodologically invalid, and we do not report cross-metric amplification factors.\n119\tQualitatively, reference VLMs show weak sensitivity: the TraceVLA reference (Phi-3-Vision) produces peak cosine distances of $0.15$--$0.19$; the NORA reference (Qwen2.5-VL) yields $0.081$ on Goal."
            }
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "session": "feishu:group:oc_9e9aef1687e6abd097aa0edaf0551ee3",
            "tool": "Read",
            "elapsed_ms": 50
