          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "720\t\\centering\n721\t\\includegraphics[width=\\columnwidth]{figures/fig_cross_architecture_attention.pdf}\n722\t\\caption{Instruction-dominant heads across layers for two architectures (OpenVLA / TraceVLA), each comparing pre-VLA and VLA-trained conditions. Despite opposite starting points---OpenVLA (Llama-2) begins with sparse attention while TraceVLA (Phi-3-V) begins with distributed attention---VLA training drives both to entry-exit concentration (L1 saturation, mid-layer suppression, L29--L31 re-engagement).}\n723\t\\end{figure}\n724\t"
            }
