          "role": "tool_result",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "971\t\\paragraph{Convergent reorganization from divergent starting points.}\n972\tReference profiles differ qualitatively: OpenVLA (Llama-2) peaks at L0 ($R^2 = 0.629$) then collapses to near-zero at mid-layers (L20: $0.086$, std $= 0.311$), while Phi-3-V peaks at L6 ($0.578 \\pm 0.018$) with gradual monotonic decline (late-layer std $= 0.068$).\n973\tAfter VLA training, both architectures reach nearly identical mid-layer peaks---OpenVLA at L9 ($R^2 = 0.637 \\pm 0.008$), TraceVLA at L11 ($0.634 \\pm 0.009$)---with $\\Delta = 0.003$ and overlapping CIs.\n974\tDeep-layer variance drops sharply with training: OpenVLA std $0.277 \\to 0.040$; Phi-3-V std $0.068 \\to 0.011$.\n975\tPeak $R^2$ values are comparable before and after training (reference peaks reach $91$--$99\\%$ of trained), but peak locations shift deeper (L0$\\to$L9; L6$\\to$L11) and profile shapes transform from architecture-specific patterns to a shared mid-layer plateau."
            }
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "session": "feishu:group:oc_9e9aef1687e6abd097aa0edaf0551ee3",
