        {
          "source_line": 736,
          "timestamp": "2026-05-29T10:30:14.090672+00:00",
          "recorded_role": "tool_result",
          "role": "tool_result",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "1084\tTask-specific fine-tuning eliminates L31 re-engagement (18 $\\to$ 0 heads; \\S\\ref{sec:openvla_routing}), consistent with exit-layer attention serving multi-task flexibility ($N{=}2$).\n1085\tTraceVLA~\\cite{zheng2024tracevla} (Phi-3-V) shows consistent entry-exit attention concentration from an opposite starting point (\\S\\ref{sec:openvla_routing}).\n1086\tThe $2 {\\times} 2$ trained-vs-reference comparison reveals a consistent reorganization pattern: reference OpenVLA collapses from L0 ($R^2 = 0.629$) to near-zero at mid-layers (L20: $0.086$, std $= 0.277$), while reference Phi-3-V peaks at L6 ($0.578$) with gradual decline (std $= 0.068$)---qualitatively opposite reference landscapes.\n1087\tYet training drives both to nearly identical mid-layer peaks ($0.637$ vs.\\ $0.634$, $\\Delta = 0.003$) with stabilized deep-layer variance (OpenVLA std $0.277 \\to 0.040$; Phi-3-V $0.068 \\to 0.011$).\n1088\tThis consistent outcome from divergent starting points suggests that mid-layer action specialization is a consistent convergence pattern of VLA training, not an architectural artifact."
            }
          ],
          "metadata": {
